#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengiraan kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing the number of iterations"
msgstr "Memilih bilangan iterasi"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore leftarrow */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore leftarrow */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We have established that the state vector of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ in "
"Grover's algorithm remains in the two-dimensional subspace spanned by "
"$\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ once the initialization step "
"has been performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita telah menetapkan bahawa vektor keadaan daftar $\\mathsf{Q}$ dalam "
"algoritma Grover kekal dalam subruang dua dimensi yang dijangkau oleh "
"$\\vert A_0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ setelah langkah inisialisasi "
"dilakukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The goal is to find an element $x\\in A_1,$ and this goal will be accomplished if we can obtain the state $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — for if we measure this state, we're guaranteed to get a measurement outcome $x\\in A_1.$\n"
"Given that the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ after $t$ iterations in step 2 is\n"
msgstr ""
"Matlamatnya adalah untuk mencari unsur $x\\in A_1,$ dan matlamat ini akan dicapai jika kita dapat memperoleh keadaan $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — kerana jika kita mengukur keadaan ini, kita dijamin mendapat hasil ukuran $x\\in A_1.$\n"
"Memandangkan keadaan $\\mathsf{Q}$ selepas $t$ iterasi dalam langkah 2 adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "we should choose $t$ so that\n"
msgstr "kita harus memilih $t$ supaya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A_1 \\vert G^t \\vert u \\rangle =\n"
"\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A_1 \\vert G^t \\vert u \\rangle =\n"
"\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is as close to $1$ as possible in absolute value, to maximize the probability to obtain $x\\in A_1$ from the measurement.\n"
"For any angle $\\theta \\in (0,2\\pi),$ the value $\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)$ *oscillates* as $t$ increases, though it is not necessarily periodic — there's no guarantee that we'll ever get the same value twice.\n"
msgstr ""
"sedekat mungkin kepada $1$ dalam nilai mutlak, untuk memaksimumkan kebarangkalian memperoleh $x\\in A_1$ daripada pengukuran.\n"
"Untuk mana-mana sudut $\\theta \\in (0,2\\pi),$ nilai $\\sin((2t + 1)\\theta)$ *berosilasi* apabila $t$ meningkat, walaupun ia tidak semestinya berkala — tiada jaminan kita akan mendapat nilai yang sama dua kali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naturally, in addition to making the probability of obtaining an element $x\\in A_1$ from the measurement large, we would also like to choose $t$ to be as small as possible, because $t$ applications of the operation $G$ requires $t$ queries to the function $f.$\n"
"Because we're aiming to make $\\sin( (2t + 1) \\theta)$ close to $1$ in absolute value, a natural way to do this is to choose $t$ so that\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu, selain daripada menjadikan kebarangkalian memperoleh unsur $x\\in A_1$ daripada pengukuran besar, kita juga ingin memilih $t$ sekecil mungkin, kerana $t$ penggunaan operasi $G$ memerlukan $t$ pertanyaan kepada fungsi $f.$\n"
"Kerana kita bertujuan untuk menjadikan $\\sin( (2t + 1) \\theta)$ hampir kepada $1$ dalam nilai mutlak, cara semula jadi untuk melakukan ini adalah dengan memilih $t$ supaya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(2t + 1) \\theta \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(2t + 1) \\theta \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Solving for $t$ yields\n"
msgstr "Menyelesaikan untuk $t$ menghasilkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} - \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} - \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, $t$ must be an integer, so we won't necessarily be able to hit "
"this value exactly — but what we can do is to take the closest integer to "
"this value, which is\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu, $t$ mesti berupa integer, jadi kita tidak semestinya dapat "
"mencapai nilai ini dengan tepat — tetapi apa yang boleh kita lakukan adalah "
"mengambil integer yang paling hampir dengan nilai ini, iaitu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the recommended number of iterations for Grover's algorithm.\n"
"As we proceed with the analysis, we'll see that the closeness of this integer to the target value naturally affects the performance of the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah bilangan iterasi yang disyorkan untuk algoritma Grover.\n"
"Apabila kita meneruskan analisis, kita akan lihat bahawa kedekatan integer ini dengan nilai sasaran secara semula jadi mempengaruhi prestasi algoritma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(As an aside, if the target value $\\pi/(4\\theta) - 1/2$ happens to be "
"exactly half-way between two integers, this expression of $t$ is what we get"
" by rounding up. We could alternatively round down, which makes sense to do "
"because it means one fewer query — but this is secondary and unimportant for"
" the sake of the lesson.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Sebagai catatan tambahan, jika nilai sasaran $\\pi/(4\\theta) - 1/2$ "
"kebetulan tepat di tengah-tengah antara dua integer, ungkapan $t$ ini adalah"
" apa yang kita dapat dengan membundarkan ke atas. Kita boleh membundarkan ke"
" bawah sebagai alternatif, yang masuk akal dilakukan kerana ia bermakna satu"
" pertanyaan lebih sedikit — tetapi ini adalah perkara kedua dan tidak "
"penting untuk tujuan pelajaran.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recalling that the value of the angle $\\theta$ is given by the formula\n"
msgstr "Dengan mengingat bahawa nilai sudut $\\theta$ diberikan oleh formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we see that the recommended number of iterations $t$ depends on the number of strings in $A_1.$\n"
"This presents a challenge if we don't know how many solutions we have, as we'll discuss later.\n"
msgstr ""
"kita melihat bahawa bilangan iterasi yang disyorkan $t$ bergantung kepada bilangan rentetan dalam $A_1.$\n"
"Ini menimbulkan cabaran jika kita tidak tahu berapa banyak penyelesaian yang ada, seperti yang akan kita bincangkan kemudian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unique search {#unique-search}"
msgstr "Carian unik {#unique-search}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's focus on the situation in which there's a single string $x$ such that $f(x)=1.$\n"
"Another way to say this is that we're considering an instance of the *Unique search* problem.\n"
"In this case we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari kita fokus pada situasi di mana terdapat satu rentetan tunggal $x$ sedemikian rupa sehingga $f(x)=1.$\n"
"Cara lain untuk menyatakannya ialah kita sedang mempertimbangkan suatu contoh masalah *carian Unik*.\n"
"Dalam kes ini kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which can be conveniently approximated as\n"
msgstr "yang boleh dianggarkan secara mudah sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr) \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}} \\biggr) \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"when $N$ gets large.\n"
"If we substitute $\\theta = 1/\\sqrt{N}$ into the expression\n"
msgstr ""
"apabila $N$ menjadi besar.\n"
"Jika kita gantikan $\\theta = 1/\\sqrt{N}$ ke dalam ungkapan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "we obtain\n"
msgstr "kita memperoleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{N} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{N} \\Bigr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recalling that $t$ is not only the number of times the operation $G$ is "
"performed, but also the number of queries to the function $f$ required by "
"the algorithm, we see that we're on track to obtaining an algorithm that "
"requires $O(\\sqrt{N})$ queries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengingat bahawa $t$ bukan sahaja bilangan kali operasi $G$ "
"dilakukan, tetapi juga bilangan pertanyaan kepada fungsi $f$ yang diperlukan"
" oleh algoritma, kita melihat bahawa kita sedang menuju kepada algoritma "
"yang memerlukan $O(\\sqrt{N})$ pertanyaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll investigate how well the recommended choice of $t$ works.\n"
"The probability that the final measurement results in the unique solution can be expressed explicitly as\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan menyiasat seberapa baik pilihan $t$ yang disyorkan berfungsi.\n"
"Kebarangkalian bahawa pengukuran akhir menghasilkan penyelesaian unik boleh dinyatakan secara eksplisit sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) = \\sin^2 \\bigl( (2t + 1) \\theta \\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) = \\sin^2 \\bigl( (2t + 1) \\theta \\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first argument, $N,$ refers to the number of items we're searching over, and the second argument, which is $1$ in this case, refers to the number of solutions.\n"
"A bit later we'll use the same notation more generally, where there are multiple solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hujah pertama, $N,$ merujuk kepada bilangan item yang kita cari, dan hujah kedua, yang merupakan $1$ dalam kes ini, merujuk kepada bilangan penyelesaian.\n"
"Sedikit kemudian kita akan menggunakan notasi yang sama secara lebih umum, di mana terdapat pelbagai penyelesaian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a table of the probabilities of success for increasing values of $N ="
" 2^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah jadual kebarangkalian kejayaan untuk nilai $N = 2^n$ yang "
"semakin meningkat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,1)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"2\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"1024 &\t 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"2048 &\t 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"4096 &\t 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"8192 &\t 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"16384 &\t 0.9999997811\\\\\n"
"32768 &\t 0.9999868295\\\\\n"
"65536 &\t 0.9999882596\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,1)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"2\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"1024 &\t 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"2048 &\t 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"4096 &\t 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"8192 &\t 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"16384 &\t 0.9999997811\\\\\n"
"32768 &\t 0.9999868295\\\\\n"
"65536 &\t 0.9999882596\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that these probabilities are not strictly increasing.\n"
"In particular, we have an interesting anomaly when $N=4,$ where we get a solution with certainty.\n"
"It can, however, be proved in general that\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa kebarangkalian ini tidak meningkat secara ketat.\n"
"Khususnya, kita mempunyai anomali menarik apabila $N=4,$ di mana kita mendapat penyelesaian dengan kepastian.\n"
"Namun, secara umum boleh dibuktikan bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) \\geq 1 - \\frac{1}{N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,1) \\geq 1 - \\frac{1}{N}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for all $N,$ so the probability of success goes to $1$ in the limit as $N$ becomes large, as the values above seem to suggest.\n"
"This is good!\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk semua $N,$ jadi kebarangkalian kejayaan menuju kepada $1$ dalam had apabila $N$ menjadi besar, seperti yang dicadangkan oleh nilai di atas.\n"
"Ini bagus!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"But notice, however, that even a weak bound such as $p(N,1) \\geq 1/2$ establishes the utility of Grover's algorithm.\n"
"For whatever measurement outcome $x$ we obtain from running the procedure, we can always check to see if $f(x) = 1$ using a single query to $f.$\n"
"And if we fail to obtain the unique string $x$ for which $f(x) = 1$ with probability at most $1/2$ by running the procedure once, then after $m$ independent runs of the procedure we will have failed to obtain this unique string $x$ with probability at most $2^{-m}.$\n"
"That is, using $O(m \\sqrt{N})$ queries to $f,$ we'll obtain the unique solution $x$ with probability at least $1 - 2^{-m}.$\n"
"Using the better bound $p(N,1) \\geq 1 - 1/N$ reveals that the probability to find $x\\in A_1$ using this method is actually at least $1 - N^{-m}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tapi perhatikan, walau bagaimanapun, bahawa walaupun sempadan lemah seperti $p(N,1) \\geq 1/2$ membuktikan kegunaan algoritma Grover.\n"
"Untuk apa jua hasil ukuran $x$ yang kita peroleh daripada menjalankan prosedur, kita sentiasa boleh menyemak sama ada $f(x) = 1$ menggunakan satu pertanyaan kepada $f.$\n"
"Dan jika kita gagal memperoleh rentetan unik $x$ yang $f(x) = 1$ dengan kebarangkalian paling banyak $1/2$ dengan menjalankan prosedur sekali, maka selepas $m$ jalan bebas prosedur kita akan gagal memperoleh rentetan unik $x$ ini dengan kebarangkalian paling banyak $2^{-m}.$\n"
"Iaitu, menggunakan $O(m \\sqrt{N})$ pertanyaan kepada $f,$ kita akan memperoleh penyelesaian unik $x$ dengan kebarangkalian sekurang-kurangnya $1 - 2^{-m}.$\n"
"Menggunakan sempadan yang lebih baik $p(N,1) \\geq 1 - 1/N$ mendedahkan bahawa kebarangkalian untuk mencari $x\\in A_1$ menggunakan kaedah ini sebenarnya sekurang-kurangnya $1 - N^{-m}.$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple solutions {#multiple-solutions}"
msgstr "Pelbagai penyelesaian {#multiple-solutions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the number of elements in $A_1$ varies, so too does the angle $\\theta,$ which can have a significant effect on the algorithm's probability of success.\n"
"For the sake of brevity, let's write $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ to denote the number of solutions, and as before we'll assume that $s\\geq 1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila bilangan unsur dalam $A_1$ berubah, begitu juga sudut $\\theta,$ yang boleh memberi kesan ketara kepada kebarangkalian kejayaan algoritma.\n"
"Untuk ringkas, mari kita tulis $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ untuk menandakan bilangan penyelesaian, dan seperti sebelum ini kita akan anggap bahawa $s\\geq 1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a motivating example, let's imagine that we have $s = 4$ solutions rather than a single solution, as we considered above.\n"
"This means that\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh motivasi, mari kita bayangkan kita mempunyai $s = 4$ penyelesaian berbanding satu penyelesaian tunggal, seperti yang kita pertimbangkan di atas.\n"
"Ini bermakna\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is approximately double the angle we had in the $\\vert A_1 \\vert = 1$ case when $N$ is large.\n"
"Suppose that we didn't know any better, and selected the same value of $t$ as in the unique solution setting:\n"
msgstr ""
"yang kira-kira dua kali ganda sudut yang kita ada dalam kes $\\vert A_1 \\vert = 1$ apabila $N$ besar.\n"
"Andaikan kita tidak tahu lebih baik, dan memilih nilai $t$ yang sama seperti dalam tetapan penyelesaian unik:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Biggl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\sin^{-1}\\bigl(1/\\sqrt{N}\\bigr)}\\Biggr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Biggl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\sin^{-1}\\bigl(1/\\sqrt{N}\\bigr)}\\Biggr\\rfloor.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The effect will be catastrophic as the following table of probabilities "
"reveals.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesannya akan menjadi bencana seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh jadual "
"kebarangkalian berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & \\text{Success probability}\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.2500000000\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.0122070313\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.0203807689\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.0144530758\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.0000705058\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.0019310741\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.0023009083\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.0000077506\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.0002301502\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.0003439882\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.0000007053\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.0000533810\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.0000472907\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & \\text{Kebarangkalian kejayaan}\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t& 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t& 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t& 0.2500000000\\\\\n"
"32\t& 0.0122070313\\\\\n"
"64\t& 0.0203807689\\\\\n"
"128\t& 0.0144530758\\\\\n"
"256\t& 0.0000705058\\\\\n"
"512\t& 0.0019310741\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.0023009083\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.0000077506\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.0002301502\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.0003439882\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.0000007053\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.0000533810\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.0000472907\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This time the probability of success goes to $0$ as $N$ goes to infinity.\n"
"This happens because we're effectively rotating twice as fast as we did when there was a unique solution, so we end up zooming past the target $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ and landing near $-\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kali ini kebarangkalian kejayaan menuju kepada $0$ apabila $N$ menuju kepada infiniti.\n"
"Ini berlaku kerana kita secara efektifnya berputar dua kali lebih cepat berbanding apabila terdapat penyelesaian unik, jadi kita terlepas sasaran $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ dan mendarat berhampiran $-\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "However, if instead we use the recommended choice of $t,$ which is\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, jika sebaliknya kita menggunakan pilihan $t$ yang disyorkan, iaitu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl( \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}} \\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then the performance will be better.\n"
"To be more precise, using this choice of $t$ leads to success with high probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"maka prestasinya akan lebih baik.\n"
"Untuk lebih tepat, menggunakan pilihan $t$ ini membawa kepada kejayaan dengan kebarangkalian tinggi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,4)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t & 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"32\t & 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"64\t & 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"128\t & 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"256\t & 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"512\t & 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.9999997811\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ll}\n"
"N & p(N,4)\\\\ \\hline\n"
"4\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"8\t & 0.5000000000\\\\\n"
"16\t & 1.0000000000\\\\\n"
"32\t & 0.9453125000\\\\\n"
"64\t & 0.9613189697\\\\\n"
"128\t & 0.9991823155\\\\\n"
"256\t & 0.9965856808\\\\\n"
"512\t & 0.9956198657\\\\\n"
"1024\t& 0.9999470421\\\\\n"
"2048\t& 0.9994480262\\\\\n"
"4096\t& 0.9994612447\\\\\n"
"8192\t& 0.9999968478\\\\\n"
"16384\t& 0.9999453461\\\\\n"
"32768\t& 0.9999157752\\\\\n"
"65536\t& 0.9999997811\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalizing what was claimed earlier, it can be proved that\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengeneralisasikan apa yang dituntut sebelum ini, boleh dibuktikan bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq 1 - \\frac{s}{N},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq 1 - \\frac{s}{N},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where we're using the notation suggested earlier: $p(N,s)$ denotes the "
"probability that Grover's algorithm run for $t$ iterations reveals a "
"solution when there are $s$ solutions in total out of $N$ possibilities.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana kita menggunakan notasi yang dicadangkan sebelum ini: $p(N,s)$ "
"menandakan kebarangkalian bahawa algoritma Grover yang dijalankan selama $t$"
" iterasi mendedahkan satu penyelesaian apabila terdapat $s$ penyelesaian "
"secara keseluruhan daripada $N$ kemungkinan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lower bound of $1 - s/N$ on the probability of success is slightly peculiar in that more solutions implies a worse lower bound — but under the assumption that $s$ is significantly smaller than $N,$ we nevertheless conclude that the probability of success is reasonably high.\n"
"As before, the mere fact that $p(N,s)$ is reasonably large implies the algorithm's usefulness.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan bawah $1 - s/N$ pada kebarangkalian kejayaan ini agak pelik dalam erti kata bahawa lebih banyak penyelesaian bermakna sempadan bawah yang lebih lemah — tetapi dengan andaian bahawa $s$ jauh lebih kecil daripada $N,$ kita tetap menyimpulkan bahawa kebarangkalian kejayaan agak tinggi.\n"
"Seperti sebelum ini, hakikat semata-mata bahawa $p(N,s)$ agak besar menyiratkan kegunaan algoritma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It also happens to be the case that\n"
msgstr "Ia juga berlaku bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq \\frac{s}{N}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(N,s) \\geq \\frac{s}{N}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lower bound describes the probability that a string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ selected uniformly at random is a solution — so Grover's algorithm always does at least as well as random guessing.\n"
"(In fact, when $t=0,$ Grover's algorithm *is* random guessing.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan bawah ini menerangkan kebarangkalian bahawa rentetan $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ yang dipilih secara rawak seragam adalah satu penyelesaian — jadi algoritma Grover selalu melakukan sekurang-kurangnya sebaik meneka secara rawak.\n"
"(Sebenarnya, apabila $t=0,$ algoritma Grover *adalah* meneka secara rawak.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's take a look at the number of iterations (and hence the number of "
"queries)\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita lihat bilangan iterasi (dan seterusnya bilangan "
"pertanyaan)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t = \\Bigl\\lfloor \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta}\\Bigr\\rfloor,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For every $\\alpha \\in [0,1],$ it is the case that $\\sin^{-1}(\\alpha)\\geq \\alpha,$\n"
"and so\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk setiap $\\alpha \\in [0,1],$ adalah benar bahawa $\\sin^{-1}(\\alpha)\\geq \\alpha,$\n"
"dan oleh itu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\right) \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}\\right) \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{s}{N}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that\n"
msgstr "Ini menyiratkan bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4\\theta} \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This translates to a savings in the number of queries as $s$ grows.\n"
"In particular, the number of queries required is\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini diterjemahkan kepada penjimatan dalam bilangan pertanyaan apabila $s$ bertumbuh.\n"
"Khususnya, bilangan pertanyaan yang diperlukan adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{N}{s}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unknown number of solutions {#unknown-number-of-solutions}"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan penyelesaian yang tidak diketahui {#unknown-number-of-solutions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the number of solutions $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ is *unknown*, then a different approach is required, for in this situation we have no knowledge of $s$ to inform our choice of $t.$\n"
"There are, in fact, multiple approaches.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bilangan penyelesaian $s = \\vert A_1 \\vert$ adalah *tidak diketahui*, maka pendekatan yang berbeza diperlukan, kerana dalam situasi ini kita tidak mempunyai pengetahuan tentang $s$ untuk memaklumkan pilihan $t$ kita.\n"
"Sebenarnya, terdapat pelbagai pendekatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "One simple approach is to choose\n"
msgstr "Satu pendekatan mudah adalah dengan memilih\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"t \\in \\Bigl\\{ 1,\\ldots,\\bigl\\lfloor\\pi\\sqrt{N}/4\\bigr\\rfloor \\Bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"t \\in \\Bigl\\{ 1,\\ldots,\\bigl\\lfloor\\pi\\sqrt{N}/4\\bigr\\rfloor \\Bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*uniformly at random*.\n"
"Selecting $t$ in this way always finds a solution (assuming one exists) with probability greater than 40%, though this is not obvious and requires an analysis that will not be included here.\n"
"It does makes sense, however, particularly when we think about the geometric picture:\n"
"rotating the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ a random number of times like this is not unlike choosing a random unit vector in the space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ for which it is likely that the coefficient of $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ is reasonably large.\n"
"By repeating this procedure and checking the outcome in the same way as described before, the probability to find a solution can be made very close to $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"*secara rawak seragam*.\n"
"Memilih $t$ dengan cara ini sentiasa menemukan penyelesaian (dengan mengandaikan terdapat satu) dengan kebarangkalian lebih daripada 40%, walaupun ini tidak jelas dan memerlukan analisis yang tidak akan dimasukkan di sini.\n"
"Namun ia masuk akal, terutamanya apabila kita memikirkan gambaran geometri:\n"
"memutar keadaan $\\mathsf{Q}$ beberapa kali secara rawak seperti ini tidak jauh berbeza daripada memilih vektor unit rawak dalam ruang yang dijangkau oleh $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ yang berkemungkinan besar pekali $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ agak besar.\n"
"Dengan mengulangi prosedur ini dan menyemak hasilnya dengan cara yang sama seperti yang dihuraikan sebelum ini, kebarangkalian untuk mencari penyelesaian boleh dijadikan sangat hampir kepada $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a refined method that finds a solution when one exists using "
"$O(\\sqrt{N/s})$ queries, even when the number of solutions $s$ is not "
"known, and requires $O(\\sqrt{N})$ queries to determine that there are no "
"solutions when $s=0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat kaedah yang lebih halus yang menemukan penyelesaian apabila "
"terdapat satu menggunakan $O(\\sqrt{N/s})$ pertanyaan, walaupun apabila "
"bilangan penyelesaian $s$ tidak diketahui, dan memerlukan $O(\\sqrt{N})$ "
"pertanyaan untuk menentukan bahawa tiada penyelesaian apabila $s=0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea is to choose $t$ uniformly at random from the set $\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}$ iteratively, for increasing values of $T.$\n"
"In particular, we can start with $T = 1$ and increase it exponentially, always terminating the process as soon as a solution is found and capping $T$ so as not to waste queries when there isn't a solution.\n"
"The process takes advantage of the fact that fewer queries are required when more solutions exist.\n"
"Some care is required, however, to balance the rate of growth of $T$ with the probability of success for each iteration.\n"
"(Taking $T \\leftarrow \\lceil \\frac{5}{4}T\\rceil$ works, for instance, as an analysis reveals.\n"
"Doubling $T,$ however, does not — this turns out to be too fast of an increase.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Idea asasnya adalah memilih $t$ secara rawak seragam daripada set $\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}$ secara berulang, untuk nilai $T$ yang semakin meningkat.\n"
"Khususnya, kita boleh mulakan dengan $T = 1$ dan meningkatkannya secara eksponen, sentiasa menamatkan proses sebaik sahaja penyelesaian ditemui dan mengehadkan $T$ supaya tidak membuang pertanyaan apabila tiada penyelesaian.\n"
"Proses ini memanfaatkan hakikat bahawa lebih sedikit pertanyaan diperlukan apabila lebih banyak penyelesaian wujud.\n"
"Namun diperlukan sedikit kehati-hatian untuk mengimbangi kadar pertumbuhan $T$ dengan kebarangkalian kejayaan untuk setiap iterasi.\n"
"(Mengambil $T \\leftarrow \\lceil \\frac{5}{4}T\\rceil$ berfungsi, misalnya, seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh analisis.\n"
"Menggandakan $T,$ walau bagaimanapun, tidak — ini ternyata terlalu cepat untuk meningkat.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The trivial cases {#the-trivial-cases}"
msgstr "Kes-kes remeh {#the-trivial-cases}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Throughout the analysis we've just gone through, we've assumed that the number of solutions is non-zero.\n"
"Indeed, by referring to the vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Sepanjang analisis yang baru kita lalui, kita telah mengandaikan bahawa bilangan penyelesaian adalah bukan sifar.\n"
"Memang, dengan merujuk kepada vektor-vektor\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we have implicitly assumed that $A_0$ and $A_1$ are both nonempty.\n"
"Here we will briefly consider what happens when one of these sets is empty.\n"
msgstr ""
"kita secara tersirat mengandaikan bahawa $A_0$ dan $A_1$ kedua-duanya tidak kosong.\n"
"Di sini kita akan mempertimbangkan secara ringkas apa yang berlaku apabila salah satu daripada set ini kosong.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we bother with an analysis, let's observe the obvious:\n"
"if every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ is a solution, then we'll see a solution when we measure; and when there aren't any solutions, we won't see one.\n"
"In some sense there's no need to go deeper than this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita sibuk dengan analisis, mari kita perhatikan yang jelas:\n"
"jika setiap rentetan $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ adalah penyelesaian, maka kita akan melihat penyelesaian apabila kita mengukur; dan apabila tiada penyelesaian, kita tidak akan melihat satu.\n"
"Dalam sesetengah hal tidak perlu pergi lebih jauh daripada ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can, however, quickly verify the mathematics for these trivial cases.\n"
"The situation where one of $A_0$ and $A_1$ is empty happens when $f$ is constant;\n"
"$A_1$ is empty when $f(x) = 0$ for every $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ and $A_0$ is empty when $f(x) = 1$ for every $x\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"This means that\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, kita boleh mengesahkan matematik untuk kes-kes remeh ini dengan cepat.\n"
"Situasi di mana salah satu daripada $A_0$ dan $A_1$ kosong berlaku apabila $f$ adalah malar;\n"
"$A_1$ kosong apabila $f(x) = 0$ untuk setiap $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ dan $A_0$ kosong apabila $f(x) = 1$ untuk setiap $x\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Ini bermakna\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert u\\rangle = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert u\\rangle = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore\n"
msgstr "dan oleh itu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f\\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f\\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert u\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\pm \\vert u\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, irrespective of the number of iterations $t$ we perform in these cases, "
"the measurements will always reveal a uniform random string "
"$x\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, tanpa mengira bilangan iterasi $t$ yang kita lakukan dalam kes-kes "
"ini, pengukuran akan sentiasa mendedahkan rentetan rawak seragam "
"$x\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
